  "annotations_dropped": [
    {
      "annotation_id": "7aad55d43cc74c0c9c5c847190f16156_41",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\n6.Regarding the scope of Habeas Corpus Petition, no doubt, the Hon'ble Supreme Court in Sunil Batra Vs. Delhi Administration case held that a Habeas Corpus Petition to conduct an enquiry is entertainable."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "e6e50fb0a83e495d9036394f2ac19faf_42",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "It is relevant to look into the ratio laid down by the Apex Court in the case of Kanu Sanyal Vs. District https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis Magistrate, Darjeeling, reported in (1973) 2 SCC 674, wherein, the following observations are made."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "b06677407e324cd1ae9bcbf44a0ef15e_43",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\nM.Munirathinam vs The State Of Tamil Nadu on 8 August, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/128568324/\n3 22.In"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "e5896ba1c70b4c58b56d041f9136edac_44",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Kanu Sanyal v. District Magistrate, Darjeeling, this Court while dealing with the writ of habeas corpus has held as follows:\n\"4."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "9961cabff268405ba440a368a13639bf_45",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "It will be seen from this brief history of the writ of habeas corpus that it is essentially a procedural writ."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "8db833ddd3bd4bb1ac7df483ff3f8bba_46",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "It deals with the machinery of Justice, not the substantive law."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "ff0105b3fbfa4a599be9907a767cb4cb_47",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The object of the writ is to secure release of a person who is illegally restrained of his liberty....\""
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "d011aa07d2154fe1924f46f1024b88f0_48",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "23. In Manubhai Ratilal Patel v. State of Gujarat and others, an order of remand was challenged before this Court."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "38b2896499ec4b6e8beda0a4623e2fc5_49",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "After referring to a large number of judgments, which we are not referring in detail since they have all been considered in this judgment, this Court held as follows:\n\"31....It is well-accepted principle that a writ of habeas corpus is not "
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "97637b2f536541288e321d8021c2f129_50",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "24. In Saurabh Kumar v. Jailor, Koneila Jail, this Court came to the conclusion that the petitioner was in judicial custody by virtue of an order passed by the judicial magistrate and, hence, could not be said to be in illegal detention."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "6f0e043102dc4d74847a44646a33f351_51",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Justice T.S. Thakur, as he then was, in his concurring judgment held as follows:\n\"22."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "191d781148e24a7f846e9dde99918664_52",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The only question with which we are concerned within the above backdrop is whether the petitioner can be said to be in the unlawful custody."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "8381c97af85e4037825679ad84326b86_53",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Our answer to that question is in the negative."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "d4954c2cd1da4d2d8866c578e5954e3f_54",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The record which we have carefully perused shows that the petitioner is an accused facing prosecution for the offences, cognizance whereof has already been taken by the competent court."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "640db8a7d45040d69d045f896fd8eb80_55",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "He is presently in custody pursuant to the order of remand made by the said Court."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "6b24043164dc4c718f7f16c8064ea7d6_56",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "A writ of habeas corpus is, in the circumstances, totally misplaced...\""
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "814ff73fa1884436a33a0438e8b22cec_57",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "25. The same view has been taken in the State of Maharashtra and Others v. Tasneem Rizwan Siddiquee wherein it was observed that no writ of habeas corpus could be issued when the detenu was in detention pursuant to an order https://www.mhc."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "a65dfff1bd37453a81ab3edf5ce69c8a_58",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "As far as the present cases are concerned, it is not disputed that the detenus are behind bars pursuant to conviction and sentence imposed upon them by a court of competent jurisdiction and confirmed by this Court, whereby they were sentenc"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "53d776cb0f1949d887f7be8bb286dbaf_59",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "7.In the present case, the learned Additional Public Prosecutor would submit that the charge sheet has already been filed and police authorities have not proposed to take the detenue under police custody."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "bb0abba67daa4b72a9ddf9220642e36d_60",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Trial has to be commenced."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "92d328220d63412a900a627108b51f6c_61",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "In these circumstances, the Writ Habeas Corpus Petition is not entertainable."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "73a64d06285d4c47b2050693a551e517_63",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "is relevant to consider that in such circumstances, if any police excessiveness or illegal acts are found, the aggrieved persons may approach the Human Rights Commission under the Protection of Human Rights Act, 1993."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "0559397591fd40d8904f4299ce6e1a07_64",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Section 12 of the Act provides the functions of the Commission."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "e5711e90c85a44728ec1b58c43452d96_65",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Section 18 contemplates steps during and after enquiry."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "af962b1001ef4aafb8db94f650054ff1_66",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "When comprehensive provisions are availabel in special enactments to redress the grievances of the aggrived persons, Writ Court cannot conduct a roving enquiry for the purpose of ascertaining the facts and circumstances warranted an urgent "
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "4d8d8eaf28ab48ebb818b99567d5b3c7_67",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Such disputed facts require an elaborate adjudication of facts through the documents and evidence."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "e52df6c0d9354de6ac9e7790ca22f073_68",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "RATIO"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Such an effort cannot be undertaken in a Habeas Corpus Petition."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "1d62e03c67774340a717f51d3acea4d3_69",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "RATIO"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Presuming that the petitioner is entitled for some relief, such reliefs are to be considered only after conducting trial nature proceedings and merely based on the averments made in the affidavit filed in support of the Habeas Corpus Petiti"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "68a0239f72994b95ae00f73c1a77a9cc_70",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "RATIO"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "In the event of forming any such opinion, the same would undoubtedly result in miscarriage of justice."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "4db4d195d7fb4dada68556d5ba050ef0_71",
      "summary_section": "decision",
      "labels": [
        "RPC"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:decision",
        "forbidden_labels:RPC",
        "suspicious_label:rpc"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\n9.That being the factum, the detenue is at liberty to approach the competent forum."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "c47e1c676f314d3e8f91eea77b294b76_72",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "RATIO"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "However, at present, the detenue is lodged at Central Prison, Cuddalore and the police authorities have not proposed to take the detenue for custody anymore in connection with the criminal case registered."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "2de1779d8fe74f5e8c807e156a7f8be0_73",
      "summary_section": "decision",
      "labels": [
        "RPC"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:decision",
        "forbidden_labels:RPC",
        "suspicious_label:rpc",
        "explicit_leakage_phrase"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [
        {
          "pattern": "\\bpetition\\s+stands\\s+disposed\\s+of\\b",
